The Legal Context Protocol is co-stewarded by Integra Ledger and AAA-ICDR. This package publishes the
conformance vectors for the connector wire — the request-signing contract a platform's connector is held
to — so that a platform can establish that its own implementation is correct without asking anyone. The
specification itself is published at https://legalcontextprotocol.org/standard and is not part of this
distribution.

This package contains no connector, no settlement logic and no credential. The `secret` every vector
carries is a PUBLISHED conformance secret by design: a vector cannot be reproduced without the key the
signature was computed under, and the value is fixed here so that any implementation can compute the same
signature and so that a control can refuse it by name.

Nothing in this package is a statement about whether any record is enforceable, binding or lawful.
